A||||1||btoth||Need to remove inside A-pillar plastic||||2||
Z||000000||btoth||10-15-2001||12:27 PM||||Got new clips for the plastic interior a-pillar panels... I could use some advice as to how to remove them without breaking anything.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Do I have to remove most of the interior trim to do it?<P>Thanks.||||reg||2
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-15-2001||01:26 PM||||Remove the lower trim piece first, then the B pillar panel.  You will have to remove the top seat belt bolt in order to get this piece off.  Then just carefully pull down the a pillar panel and your old clips will snap out of thier holders.<P>BTW  Most of my clips are gone, but the B pillar panel and the dash basically hold it up.  I think there is only one good clip left in either of mine, and that is the one about halfway down.  All the others are broken or missing.||||reg||1
